WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.750
On any given day in 2021, 27.6
million people were in forced labour,

2
00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:08.450
the ILO estimates.

3
00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:16.270
In 2023, about 260,000 women died during
and following pregnancy and childbirth.

4
00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:22.190
In 2024, Amnesty recorded
at least 1,518 executions,

5
00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:23.890
in 15 countries.

6
00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:27.570
Map them, and the patterns do not line up.

7
00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:29.250
Is it all down to poverty?

8
00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:30.190
To war?

9
00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:35.090
So why are these three violations
concentrated in such different places?

10
00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:37.270
In this mission, you'll
map each violation,

11
00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:39.830
and see how each one is measured.

12
00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:42.030
Then you'll test what drives each pattern,

13
00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:45.050
and how far the data can be trusted.

14
00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:50.090
Your mission: explain why these three
violations are concentrated in such different

15
00:00:50.140 --> 00:00:50.990
places.
